+### ADR-143, Amendment 9 (26 November 2026) — a case's ceiling is told only to a reader cleared for it (GG4j)
+
+Status: proposed by slice GG4j from the owner's rulings of 26 November 2026 (GG4b's question 5 (a), cut as its own security slice; and
+that a refusal names only the capped ceiling the board already sent that reader). It takes effect on the owner's approval line. It
+changes the words of Amendment 2 decision 3, "naming the ceiling"; no check changes.
+
+1. **What a reader is told.** A case's ceiling (the strictest highest allowed marking of what the case reads) is sent as it is only to a
+   reader cleared for it. To anyone else it is the highest marking both under it and within their clearance. Where there is no such
+   marking (a clearance the scheme does not know), none is named.
+2. **Where.** The opened board's `ceiling`; the highest allowed marking on the promotion sheet, the layer merge sheet, the drawn merge
+   sheet and each merge target (a dataset's highest allowed marking is the ceiling of every case reading it), and those sheets' marking
+   check in words. A sheet's words about one item are said only of an item its reader sees that is above that marking, so the marking
+   they name is within the reader's clearance.
+3. **A refusal.** A drawing above the ceiling is still refused, judged against the case's real ceiling. The refusal names the ceiling as
+   decision 1 gives it to that reader, which is the one the opened board sent them: Amendment 2 decision 3's "naming the ceiling" is read
+   so. The board's refusal for the deployment's highest marking (ADR-148 decision 10, "words that say the deployment's limit") names
+   that limit the same way.
+4. **Not changed.** The markings a board offers, every write check, and each refusal's code.
+5. **Open.** A refusal's code still depends on the ceiling: to a drawing marked above the reader's own clearance, the Conduit answers
+   `above_your_clearance` when the marking is within the case's ceiling and `above_the_ceiling` when it is above it, so a reader who
+   tries markings above their own can work out the ceiling. Closing it changes which refusal such a reader is given, which the owner
+   has not ruled.
+
+Tests that would fail (rule 12; `test_board_ceiling_for_the_reader.py`): `test_row_1_a_reader_below_the_ceiling_is_told_their_own_highest`,
+`test_row_3_bs_answer_is_the_same_whatever_the_ceiling_above_b_is`, `test_row_5_a_drawing_above_the_cases_real_ceiling_is_refused_as_before`,
+`test_row_5b_bs_refusal_names_only_the_ceiling_the_board_sent_b`, `test_the_boards_deployment_refusal_names_no_marking_above_the_reader`,
+`test_row_6_the_promotion_sheet_tells_a_reader_below_the_ceiling_only_their_own`, `test_row_6_the_layer_merge_sheet_opened_and_read_again`
+and `test_row_6_the_merge_targets_and_the_drawn_merge_sheet`.
